onfig: spawn.preferred_agentic_system)\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=claude; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [analyst] solution-architect (claude) (run=RUN-260728-641408, max_parallel=1)\nspawn run started: [analyst] solution-architect (claude) (run=RUN-260728-641408)\nr3 rework against reviewer verdict 02 (CHANGES REQUESTED, one blocking finding F1). The finding was independently re-verified before acceptance and CONFIRMED three ways: .spec/platform-distribution.md:103-105 mandates the Sparkle -spks/-spki Mach lookup exceptions for the sandboxed host; this repo own .research/260721_macos-self-update.md:111-113 records the identical two-value set; and codesign -d --entitlements :- across /Applications found six shipping apps carrying exactly that pattern, three of them sandboxed with those two values and nothing else. Fix: macos.host now authors com.apple.security.temporary-exception.mach-lookup.global-name as required-adjacent with the exact authored array plus a resolvedValue for bundle-level checking, portalCapability false, owner uyju7n, project-architecture attribution (attributionNote states why it is not sandbox-consequence, unlike network.client). Rule X1 added because the same spec clause bans unreviewed exception entitlements: a reviewed-exception register plus a banned set for Hardened Runtime relaxations, with get-task-allow deliberately left to A10d. Assertions A10e, A14, A15 added; R27 pins the assertion id set so it cannot silently shrink again. Two evidence notes recorded rather than smoothed over: Tailscale ships the exception while unsandboxed (so shipping-product presence is not proof of requirement), and Sparkle binary names three endpoint suffixes (-spks, -spki, -spkp) of which only two are entitled, making the two-value set deliberate. Gates: reviewer own targeted jq gate now true/exit 0 (was false/exit 1); validate_matrix.py 27 rules 598 checks exit 0; mutate.py 41/41 negative gates exit 0; 11/11 explicit r2-preservation assertions hold; check-legacy-preservation.sh exit 0; task-board validate exit 0; swift test 335 tests in 29 suites exit 0. Both harness scripts re-verified running in place from the board resource layout. No board elements created or changed; no product source, spec, or generated project modified.\nagent completed: [analyst] solution-architect (claude) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: claude (run=RUN-260728-641408, pid=58959, exit=0)\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override (preferred_agentic_system: mixed[claude,codex], config: spawn.preferred_agentic_system)\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260728-8b59cc, max_parallel=1)\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260728-8b59cc)\nagent completed: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260728-8b59cc, pid=62847, exit=0)\n2026-07-28 TASK-260728-7ii1xz AMENDMENT REQUEST (this task is the applying owner per matrix section 11). Verdict: keychain-access-groups on works.relux.tunnel.mac.tunnel KEEP PROHIBITED - promote prohibited-pending-decision to settled prohibited. The selected transport is the file-based System keychain, whose access model is per-item SecAccess ACLs, not access groups (TN3137), so the entitlement is inapplicable rather than merely unused. The provider needs no keychain entitlement: /System/Library/Sandbox/Profiles/application.sb lines 792-793 on macOS 26.5 25F71 already grant read+write on /Library/Keychains to any process holding com.apple.developer.networking.networkextension, and lines 655-656 grant the securityd Mach lookups to every sandboxed process. No new entitlement, App ID, portal capability, or C1 change. Also: M2 close OC-1 naming TASK-260728-7ii1xz; M3 downgrade OC-4 to verify-only-if-XPC-is-ever-selected since the XPC candidate was rejected; M4 no change requested on the macos.host row, recommend keep granted with purpose narrowed to iOS system of record plus macOS pre-seed staging; M5 consider a rule recording that keychain-access-groups is meaningless on the file-based path, so PureVPN shipping it cannot be used as a re-grant argument. Full rationale and evidence: TASK-260728-7ii1xz_macos-credential-transport-decision.md section 7.\n2026-07-28 TASK-260728-7ii1xz amendment addendum M6 - com.apple.security.application-groups on both macOS targets: no value change requested, but the stated PURPOSE is wrong. The matrix section 10 traceability row host-to-provider state is an App Group snapshot plus Keychain refs, and any G2 purpose text implying a shared container on macOS, are false on macOS: the user-context host and the root provider resolve DIFFERENT containers (provider home is /private/var/root). The macOS host-to-provider channel is providerConfiguration plus the app-message seed. The entitlement is left granted because a private root-context container may still have uses this task did not survey; whether it survives least privilege is a separate review under ypo7yo ownership. See TASK-260728-7ii1xz_macos-credential-transport-decision.md sections 6 and 7.\n2026-07-28 TASK-260728-7ii1xz r2 AMENDMENT PACKET (supersedes the r1 packet; verdict unchanged, field list now exhaustive). Target row: targets[key=macos.provider].entitlements[keychain-access-groups] on works.relux.tunnel.mac.tunnel. VERDICT: KEEP PROHIBITED. The selected transport is the file-based system-domain keychain, whose access model is per-item SecAccess ACL, not access groups (TN3137), so the entitlement is INAPPLICABLE to the mechanism used, not merely unnecessary. The provider needs no keychain entitlement at all: application.sb:792-793 on macOS 26.5 (25F71) already grants /Library/Keychains read+write to any com.apple.developer.networking.networkextension holder, and 655-656 grant the securityd Mach lookups to every sandboxed process. No value, no portal capability, no new App ID, no C1 change. FIELD-BY-FIELD (all five keys on the row): status prohibited-pending-decision -> prohibited; rationale -> the settled reason above citing TASK-260728-7ii1xz; evidence -> keep and add application.sb:792-793 plus checks E8-E10; resolutionOwner -> REMOVE (this task IS the resolution; a settled row naming a pending resolver reads as still-open); amendmentRule -> REMOVE and replace with M5. The amendmentRule removal is the critical one: its antecedent (transport gives the provider direct keychain access) is now TRUE while its consequent (amend to required with the group literal) is FALSE, so left in place it is a live instruction to re-grant the row on exactly the reasoning this decision refutes. M2: close OC-1 naming TASK-260728-7ii1xz as resolver. M3: keep OC-4 open, downgraded to verify-only-if-XPC-is-ever-selected. M4: macos.host keychain-access-groups - no change requested, recommend keep granted with the purpose narrowed to iOS system of record plus a macOS pre-seed staging item. M5: record the replacement rule - on macOS the file-based keychain is SecAccess-ACL controlled and keychain-access-groups applies only to the Data Protection Keychain, so a root-context provider never needs it and the presence of the key in a shipping third-party provider is not evidence it functions; the row reopens only if the provider is ever moved into a user context. M6: application-groups on both macOS targets - no value change, but the stated purpose and the section 10 traceability row implying a shared container on macOS are FALSE (host and provider resolve different containers). M7: bump revision, append a revisionLog entry naming TASK-260728-7ii1xz_reviewer-verdict-01.md and this decision, keep validate-matrix at exit 0, and check that deleting resolutionOwner/amendmentRule does not trip an exhaustive containment assertion - if one requires them it encoded the open state and must be updated in the same revision. Consider a negative gate: a prohibited row still carrying a resolutionOwner is a contradiction. See TASK-260728-7ii1xz_macos-credential-transport-decision.md section 7.\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: claude via explicit_override (preferred_agentic_system: mixed[claude,codex], config: spawn.preferred_agentic_system)\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=claude; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [analyst] solution-architect (claude) (run=RUN-260728-d6c87d, max_parallel=1)\nspawn run started: [analyst] solution-architect (claude) (run=RUN-260728-d6c87d)\nr4 rework against reviewer verdict 03 (CHANGES REQUESTED, one blocking finding F1 plus a secondary correction), and application of the TASK-260728-7ii1xz r2 amendment packet M1-M7 in the same revision because M1 and F1 touch the same two rows. F1 independently CONFIRMED against the r3 artifact. Neither of the reviewer two exits applied verbatim: 7ii1xz finished in the interim and its M6 explicitly handed the least-privilege call to this task, so the survey was done rather than the row deferred again. Verdict: com.apple.security.application-groups is PROHIBITED on all four macOS targets (production AND probe) and required on all four iOS targets - new rule G4. Basis is a grant-by-grant read of /System/Library/Sandbox/Profiles/application.sb 26.5/25F71 at lines 302-330 and 459-465, the only two places the key appears: six grants, three home-relative and broken across the root/user split, three system-wide and belonging to mechanisms this project does not use (Mac App Store group content, a group-prefixed XPC Mach service which 7ii1xz rejected as candidate C, group-prefixed POSIX IPC which nobody proposed). M6 open question about a private root-context container is answered harder than M6 expected: appsandbox-container-common and -macos at application.sb:107-108 are unconditional, so every sandboxed target already has its own container and a group container adds only sharing, which is exactly what is broken. Ceremony C1 shrank - no App Group record, no App Groups capability on any App ID - and the convenience argument evaporates rather than being demoted, because C1 already excludes all four iOS App IDs under ADR-024 and those are the records only consumers. Amendment packet applied in full: M1 all five fields including deletion of resolutionOwner and amendmentRule, M2 OC-1 closed, M3 OC-4 dormant plus new sandbox-side evidence that the Mach prefix mechanism is style-agnostic, M4 macos.host purpose narrowed as recommended, M5 rule K1, M6, M7. M7 warning checked and did not bite - the containment assertions key off status, not row metadata. Beyond the literal ask, two things stated in the handoff: the macOS PROBE rows were withheld too (leaving them would park the identical defect one row over), and the amendment packet was applied in the same revision. Secondary correction fixed and the number moved underneath it: the macos.host development allowlist is nine keys, not seven or ten, because the App Group is no longer authored. Gates: reviewer own targeted jq gate true/exit 0 (was false/exit 1); validate_matrix.py 30 rules 801 checks exit 0; mutate.py 66/66 negative gates exit 0 including one that rejects the over-correction; 15/15 r3 preservation assertions hold; check-legacy-preservation.sh exit 0; task-board validate exit 0; swift test 335 tests in 29 suites exit 0. Both harness scripts re-verified running in place from the board resource layout. Recorded not actioned: PlatformVPNIdentity.appGroupIdentifier is unsatisfiable on macOS (owner TASK-260715-1tzaed) and .spec/architecture.md:111 needs amendment. No board element created or changed; no product source, sp